WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:05.810
<b>7 years ago: Taklamakan Desert</b>

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.320
Is it good, Homare?

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:06.210
Yeah!

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.360
These are like potatoes! They're yummy!

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.760
They're called fox radishes,
and they grow in deserts.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.860
<b>Homare's Papa</b>

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.950
They help improve the immune system.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.420
When the guide stole our camels and ran away,
I didn't know what would happen to us.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.800
Everything's going to be fine.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.540
Life comes with trouble, Homare.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:27.230
When you're under survival conditions,
"knowing" is the most important thing.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.710
With knowledge, you can fill your stomach
and gain the strength to move forward.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.330
Now, tomorrow's an early day.

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:35.370
Why don't we get some sleep?

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.010
Okay, Papa!

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:47.730
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.530
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:41.790
All right.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:45.330
Let's use the scissors we found in
the abandoned house to make a knife.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.000
Resin

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.000
Ash

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.000
Rabbit Droppings

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.000
First, is this.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.520
Resin?

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:50.880
Right. We'll use this to make an adhesive.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.380
Melt a chunk of resin...

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:57.170
Mix the rabbit droppings and ash together...

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:01.260
Then add it to the resin in a ratio
of 3 parts resin to 1 part mixture.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.510
Once they've been kneaded together, it's done.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.060
That's amazing!

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.800
We'll use this to fix the grip
and sheath together temporarily.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.320
Huh? You mean it's not done?

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.150
This adhesive isn't that strong...

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.820
so I decided to make the handle out of rope.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:20.620
Yes. That's good.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:22.490
The knife is finished!

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:26.810
No. There's still shaping the handle and
sharpening the blade, so it's not quite done.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.520
And I have to make one more.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:30.370
She looks so happy.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:34.730
Can you put the leftover adhesive
on some sticks while it's still hot?

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:36.830
We can use them as torches.
They'll come in handy at night.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:37.800
Okay.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.760
<i>Homare-san is so excited!</i>

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.760
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.760
<b>Homare's party has acquired a knife x 2</b>

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:44.850
Really?

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.480
It's so hot...

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.760
Hey, Mutsu. Could you look at this?

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:57.620
Right around here, my sunburn really stings...

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.950
The skin is peeling, Asuka-san!

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:03.400
If my hair gets as long as Shion's,

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.510
I wonder if that'll keep the back
of my neck from getting sunburned.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:08.370
Oh, don't. I don't think it will suit you.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.460
I didn't ask you.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.910
The UV rays are pretty strong during the day...

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.290
It would be nice if we had some sunblock...

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.130
It would.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.250
At this rate, day by day,
we'll just get darker and darker...

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:23.460
We'll transform from lovely young girls...

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:25.740
'Sup!

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.570
...to delinquent party girls, then...

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:29.800
to desiccated husks left
out in the sun too long.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:30.560
Cough...

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.020
No!

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.950
And that's the appearance that would
be broadcast live on television...

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.190
Stop it!

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:43.110
Homare's the only one of us
who's never bothered by anything.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:54.500
<b>7 years ago: Fiji</b>

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.500
Papa, you can see underwater
even without goggles?

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.830
Yes.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.460
It varies from person to person,

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:01.350
but you can train yourself
to see underwater clearly.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:05.640
<i>I can see a lot better now than I used to.</i>

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.190
<i>That was...</i>

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:11.810
Everyone.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.310
I got a squid.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.580
What's on your face?

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.050
Squid ink?

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:20.480
You want sunblock?

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.320
Is there anything we can do?

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.810
Even without sunblock, we're...

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:35.170
<b>7 years ago: Fiji</b>

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:35.170
Homare, getting too much UV isn't good.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:39.840
If you do, it can lead to a
decline in your immune system.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.750
Which is why...

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.610
we'll take the ink from the squid we caught...

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:47.990
and spread it on our skin.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:53.810
Squid ink works just as well
as commercial sunblock.

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:56.580
Then we don't have to worry, right?

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.520
So there you go.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.830
That's it! Put some on me, too!

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:03.120
Yeah! And me! Put some on me!

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.650
In that case, me, too...

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.780
It squirted ink earlier, so...
there's only enough for one.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.170
Ready, and...

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:12.540
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:14.900
My beautiful, pale skin...

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:16.170
There. All done.

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:19.280
I'm sorry no one else could have this done.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:20.460
Wow...

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:22.660
It does smell a little fishy, doesn't it?

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:23.630
I don't think I need that after all...

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:23.990
Well, it is from a squid.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.040
Me neither...

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.360
But I feel like it's working!

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:27.580
H-Hey!

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:30.350
Aren't there any other ways to make sunblock?

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.510
Let's see...

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.330
This would probably work.

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:35.440
Seaweed?

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.190
Yeah.

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:38.870
It isn't as effective as squid ink, but...

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:40.310
it's better than not having any at all.

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:43.170
Things without shells that
live along the seashore

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:48.330
excrete a mucus at low tide to
prevent drying out from the UV rays.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.370
The slime from seaweed
has similar properties.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.020
Boil the crushed seaweed...

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:57.370
Once the properties have
been extracted, allow it to cool.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:58.710
It should be just about ready.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.160
Yes.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.970
It's become nice and viscous.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:05.960
Yay! Now I can have my lovely pale skin back!

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.900
We'll strain this through a shirt.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.300
Asuka, help me.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:09.930
Sure!

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:13.650
All right, Shion. Can you pour it in here?

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:15.720
The can will be slippery. Be careful.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:17.600
Leave it to me.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.100
I'll be just fine—

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.440
Look out!

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:25.970
Our sunblock!

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:28.240
I said to be careful, didn't I?

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.160
I-I-I'm so sorry!

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.410
Honestly.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.080
Oh, hold on! Stay just like that!

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:37.770
What are you doing?

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:40.790
Well, you know... I just
thought it was a waste...

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:42.670
What is this?

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:45.700
Everyone but me has perfect UV defenses.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.720
Wasn't it Shion-san who spilled it?

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:51.090
Shion. What about this?

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.430
What is it?

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:54.560
Dried squid liver.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.850
The fat from this can serve as sunblock, too.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:00.270
Homare-san...

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:01.830
Isn't that wonderful?

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:03.400
Now we all have some.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.980
No!

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.280
This reeks!

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.820
It reeks of squid!

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.720
It really stinks...

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.570
Sh-Shion! Stay away!

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.490
<i>Looks like everything worked out.</i>

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.490
It really smells!

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:16.490
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.930
Really?

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:23.000
There wasn't anything in the traps today.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:25.630
What's wrong?

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.350
Something in my clothes!

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:28.640
Ow...

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:30.420
This is...

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.470
Looks like a horsefly bite.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:35.940
You can just leave it and it should...

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:42.310
<b>6 years ago: Botswana Wetlands</b>

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:45.240
Homare, your legs must
feel pretty gross, right?

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:47.120
Should we take a little break to dry off?

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:48.940
I'm fine with this much.

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:52.370
Homare. Under survival conditions,

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:55.130
you should not underestimate
the effects of discomfort and stress.

00:07:57.230 --> 00:08:01.530
Even for the smallest things,
if you can fix it, you should.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.290
What is that?

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.250
The sap from a common dandelion.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:12.170
It works well on bug bites.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:15.800
Oh! I think it hurts a little less!

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:18.500
Thank you so much, Homare-san!

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:20.600
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:23.260
I'm saying that we need it!

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:23.860
Huh?

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:25.730
No we don't! This stupid thing...

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.500
We decided to make a new hammock, didn't we?

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.230
What's wrong?

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:31.030
Homare! Just listen...

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:33.530
Shion says we should make a drying rack.

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:37.490
Leaving my underthings to dry
in a place like that, I'd rather die!

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.010
What's it matter anyway?

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:41.480
It's not like there's anyone here to see!

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.470
<i>P-Papa...</i>

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:48.540
<i>Sorry to ask at a time like this...</i>

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:54.050
<b>5 years ago: Patagonia</b>

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:53.540
What is it, Homare?

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:58.180
If I have to go pee while we're
climbing, what should I do?

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:00.540
Is that all?

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:04.260
Obviously, you just go in your pants.

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:06.950
But what if I have to p—

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:08.110
Poop, too!

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:12.330
Under survival conditions,
embarrassment is not necessary!

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:13.940
Papa!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:15.990
<i>You're so cool!</i>

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:21.750
If we had a drying rack we could
dry them properly in the sun.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:25.170
No! The hammock comes first!

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.520
Nice, Asuka.

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:32.220
Very nice.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:36.470
Under survival conditions,
embarrassment is not necessary.

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:44.210
Now we can finally stop sleeping on the sand!

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:46.390
We need to build a roof soon, too.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.180
Say, Homare-san.

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:50.560
Would it be possible to make perfume?

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:54.050
It wouldn't be impossible, but... why?

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:56.740
Is what I'm asking so strange?

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:58.580
Well, I mean...

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:00.370
Are you worried about how you smell?

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.110
Let's see...

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:02.200
H-Hey, wait!

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.290
Listen, Homare...

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.750
Before we get home, take a bath.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.660
After all, we've been in a hut in
the mountains for 30 days

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:16.030
and we haven't taken a bath once.

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:19.280
If we go back like this,
Mama will get super angry, right?

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:23.430
But we don't smell at all.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.650
That's not quite right, Homare.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.590
It's called olfactory fatigue.

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:33.170
The human sense of smell is easily fatigued
and we even get used to smells we hate.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:34.820
Which means...

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:39.410
We stink! Both of us! We
just don't realize it!

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:42.820
It's all right, Shion.

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:44.260
Really?

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:45.450
There's no need to worry...

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:47.660
we all stink.

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:50.790
No!

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.460
Let's go back to the hot spring again...

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:56.490
You know, it's dumb
to bring it up now, but...

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:59.720
Homare, you really know
a lot about survival situations.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:00.750
Yeah.

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:03.540
Ever since I was little,
I traveled all over with my dad

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:05.430
and he taught me all kinds of things.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:09.020
In a way, it was like a special
program for gifted students.

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:12.680
And thanks to that, you've
helped us in so many ways.

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:14.820
We'll have to thank your father.

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.670
Well, no matter the situation, Papa—

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:20.780
my dad's teachings are always right.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:24.440
<i>A dad complex?</i>

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:29.090
Next time, Case 10:
 "Honey Bee."
